    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/Playbooks/PlaybookRunToolsAuthTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Start returns { runId, status, consoleLink } within 5 s with a slow fake engine; status returns running, then completed with a result summary.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A retried start with the same idempotencyKey and caller returns the same runId; the engine is invoked once.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: each refusal 007's method produces (playbook not usable, document not accessible, parameter policy) returns isError with the REST reasonCode and starts nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: user B's runId and a random runId return byte-identical not-found results for user A.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Status for a run absent from memory is read from the durable record (005's store faked at its boundary).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ArchTests and conformance pass; publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-05, FR-13, FR-14, NFR-06. Two adversarial-verifier passes (auth). uac-r2 reviews; ontology-r1 reviewed 007. The restart check on dev runs in 039.</notes>

